  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;be the reflection of a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> with respect to the plane given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math><br />where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;are real parameters and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;are the unit vectors along the three positive coordinate axes. If the position vectors of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;respectively, then which of the following is/are TRUE?"
  },
